{"agent_mode": null, "bash_calls": 2, "candidate_provenance": null, "checker_exit": 0, "checker_stderr": "", "checker_stdout": "round_money rounds half up; other helpers intact\nOBENCH_VERDICT: pass\n", "checker_workspace_files": {"pricing/__init__.py": {"bytes": 0, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"}, "pricing/money.py": {"bytes": 644, "mtime": 1791870399.2386978, "sha256": "65026e65c38dd655b21a86a49df1425d5c65981e986e1747121e8072ac6048dd"}, "tests/test_round_money.py": {"bytes": 404, "mtime": 1791870405.2549398, "sha256": "7153032eb993a3020cdce2609a64c8a4e559f95fa71ae594cdcafb5625222d50"}, "tests/test_split.py": {"bytes": 101, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "f21bbe9cf15cf7f51ff9f71318aca4794c29f5d66cb9ae2aa0d4c919043d9bcf"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/27517f255bc0f6927f6358a38d2c34b2efe166af/omp", "-p", "`round_money(2.675)` returns `2.67` but customers expect `2.68`. Fix it.\n", "--mode", "json", "--provider", "vertex-anthropic", "--model", "claude-opus-5-5", "--yolo", "--session-dir", "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/aa38/omp-938/transcripts/without/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/1/session"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 2, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/aa38/omp-938/cells/without/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/1/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/18.1.8 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/27517f255bc0f6927f6358a38d2c34b2efe166af/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Fixed: `round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`.\n\n**Cause:** the float `2.675` is actually stored as `2.67499999\u2026`, so Python's built-in `round(x, 2)` correctly rounds that stored value down. The docstring promised half-up rounding, but floats can't do it reliably.\n\n**Fix** in `pricing/money.py`: `round_money` now converts the number with `Decimal(repr(x))`, which gives the shortest decimal string that turns back into the same float (`\"2.675\"`). It then rounds to cents with `quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP)` and returns a float, so its return type is unchanged. `add_vat` uses it, so VAT amounts get the same fix.\n\n**Checked:**\n- `2.675\u21922.68`, `1.005\u21921.01`, `0.125\u21920.13`, `2.665\u21922.67`, `1.234\u21921.23`.\n- `-2.675\u2192-2.68`: negative halves round away from zero.\n- `add_vat(10)\u219212.0`.\n- I added `tests/test_round_money.py` to cover the halves that rounded down before. pytest isn't installed here, so I called the test functions directly; the new tests and the existing `test_split` pass.\n\n**One limit:** the result is a float, so it is the closest float to the rounded cents (e.g. `2.68` prints as `2.68` but isn't exactly that in binary). If prices are ever summed or compared exactly, the better long-term change is to carry `Decimal` or whole cents (integers) end to end.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 8, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 86317, "requests_cache_write": 142060, "requests_cost_usd": 0.7708354, "requests_count": 8, "requests_input_uncached": 18, "requests_output": 2160, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-bugfix-regress:claude-opus-5-5:trial1", "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 0, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-13T05:46:24.439427+00:00", "subagen